🚽 Test case: #197 -- chaining `.` through a pointer-typed struct/union
🚽 FIELD (`a.next.val` where `next` is `gang Node *`) now follows the
🚽 pointer, the field counterpart of #196's pointer-typed VARIABLE base.
🚽 Exercises read (a.next.val), write-through (a.next.val = 99), and
🚽 aliasing back to the pointee (b.val reflects the write) -- proving the
🚽 chain resolves to b's real storage, not a copy.
gang Node {
    rizz val;
    gang Node *next;
};

skibidi main {
    gang Node a;
    gang Node b;
    a.val = 1;
    b.val = 2;
    a.next = &b;
    yapping("%d", a.next.val);
    a.next.val = 99;
    yapping("%d", a.next.val);
    yapping("%d", b.val);
}
